{"id": "f5b305e6-893a-4a01-af79-6b9d7ab346d5", "timestamp": "2026-10-19T23:00:43.589986", "source": "agent", "parent_id": null, "system_prompt": {"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "Collaborate with the researcher to develop an experiment design for the original task. First inspect the masked repository and supplied inputs, then use end_researcher_turn with stage=plan to propose an approach, consequential choices and uncertainties. Wait for explicit researcher approval before developing the full design. After approval, hand off stage=result with the complete design in answer, supported by rationale, controls, feasible checks and repository observations in evidence. State assumptions separately from fixed task requirements. No executed experiment or invented outcome is required for this design-only task. Use inspect_repository and execute_check for exploration. Share concrete findings: private tool output is not automatically sent to the researcher. Revise when needed; do not invent objections or ambiguities to extend the conversation. The researcher decides when to stop."}, "tools": [{"description": "List a repository directory or read a text file. Paths are relative to the task workspace.", "action_type": "InspectRepositoryAction", "observation_type": "BenchmarkObservation", "annotations": null, "meta": null, "kind": "InspectRepositoryTool", "title": "inspect_repository"}, {"description": "Run a shell command in the isolated task workspace. Use small exploratory checks before submitting your plan.", "action_type": "ExecuteCheckAction", "observation_type": "BenchmarkObservation", "annotations": null, "meta": null, "kind": "ExecuteCheckTool", "title": "execute_check"}, {"description": "Yield a proposed approach (stage=plan) or completed experiment design (stage=result), with evidence, assumptions and uncertainties. The researcher decides when to finish.", "action_type": "ReviewHandoffAction", "observation_type": "BenchmarkObservation", "annotations": null, "meta": null, "kind": "ReviewHandoffTool", "title": "end_researcher_turn"}], "dynamic_context": {"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "<CURRENT_DATETIME>\nThe current date and time is: 2026-10-19T23:00\n</CURRENT_DATETIME>"}, "kind": "SystemPromptEvent"}
{"id": "d3e53d35-b8ce-4e81-b66e-142c5c6881b1", "timestamp": "2026-10-19T23:00:43.592782", "source": "user", "parent_id": "f5b305e6-893a-4a01-af79-6b9d7ab346d5", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"Привет! Let's start with inspection only — no full design yet. Context: this is a design-only task (track.md) comparing the gradient/autograd graph complexity of Adam optimizer update steps when operations are fused (TorchOpt-style) versus rendered with TorchViz.\\n\\nPlease do the following and report back:\\n\\n1. Inspect the /workspace repository: list top-level contents, look for any README, docs, notebooks, or code mentioning TorchOpt, TorchViz, functorch/vmap, Adam, or graph visualization. Report what is actually present — do not assume packages or files exist.\\n\\n2. Inspect the environment: confirm available Python version and whether torch, torchviz, torchopt (or related packages like functorch, torch.func) are importable or installed. If nothing is preinstalled, just say so — feasibility notes will need to account for that.\\n\\n3. Based on what you find, propose ONLY a high-level approach for the experiment design: how you would operationally define and measure \\\"graph complexity\\\" and \\\"interpretability\\\" (e.g., node/edge counts, graph depth, number of intermediate ops, readability of visualization), what comparison setup you'd use (same model/loss, fused vs unfused Adam step), and what you'd render/analyze.\\n\\n4. List the consequential assumptions and uncertainties in your proposal (e.g., what \\\"fused\\\" means in TorchOpt's implementation, whether TorchViz can even visualize optimizer-internal ops or only autograd graphs of forward passes, hardware/library version constraints).\\n\\nDo not write the full experiment design, run anything, or fabricate results. Just inspection, a sketch of the approach, and your assumptions. Keep it concise and concrete.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"Does fusing operations within the Adam optimizer (as done in TorchOpt) result in a less complex and more interpretable gradient graph compared to the output from TorchViz?\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 224, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null, "reasoning_content": null, "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "critic_result": null, "kind": "MessageEvent"}
